/-!
# Derived completeness along the ideal sheaf generated by finitely many global sections

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site, let `f_1, …, f_r` be global sections of `𝒪` and let
`ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r) ⊂ 𝒪` be the sheaf of ideals they generate. This file proves that an object
`L` of `D(𝒪)` is **derived complete along `ℐ`** as soon as `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_{f_i}, K) = 0` for
each generator: the condition at the finitely many generators implies the condition of
[Stacks, Tag 0999] at every local section of `ℐ` over every object of the site.

This is the half of the `hΦ` hypothesis of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion` that is about the
ideal sheaf rather than about the Čech complex, and it is proved here for an arbitrary `L`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.memVanishingIdeal_sumGlobalSection` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.memVanishingIdeal_of_eq_sum_mul`: the vanishing locus of
  [Stacks, Tag 0998] contains every finite sum of its members, and hence every `𝒪`-linear
  combination of them with coefficients taken over a terminal object of the site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedCompleteAt_terminalSectionToEnd_of_memVanishingIdeal`:
  the implication (1) ⇒ (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0997] in the spelling the derived-completeness
  predicate of [Stacks, Tag 0999] uses, namely at the scalar
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.terminalSectionToEnd` of a section over a terminal object.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal_over` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.memVanishingIdeal_over_of_isDerivedComplete`: for an **arbitrary**
  sheaf of ideals, the passage between the predicate of [Stacks, Tag 0999] and membership of
  every local section of the ideal in the vanishing locus of the corresponding restriction. This
  is the generic part of the main result, and the form in which any proof of derived completeness
  along an ideal sheaf meets [Stacks, Tag 0998].
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal`:
  **the main result.** If each generator lies in the vanishing locus of `L`, then `L` is derived
  complete along `ℐ`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.memVanishingIdeal_completionFunctor_obj` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_completionFunctor_obj`:
  **the `hΦ` hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 099F], discharged** — every Čech completion
  `K^∧ = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f), K)` is derived complete along `ℐ`. The first is the vanishing at
  the generators, from the base change of the Čech complex; the second is the main result above
  applied to it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_of_comm`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 099F] with `hΦ` and `hη` both discharged**, so that `hcomm` — that the
  completion functor carries `K ⟶ K^∧` to `K^∧ ⟶ (K^∧)^∧` — is its only remaining hypothesis.
  That hypothesis is now proved too, in `GeneratedIdealAdjoint.lean`, and the unconditional
  conclusion is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf` there;
  this file stops at the reduction.

## The argument

Fix an object `U` and a section `x` of `ℐ` over `U`. What has to be produced is
`T(L|_U, x) = 0`, which by the implication (1) ⇒ (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0997] — read at the
localized ringed site `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.over X U`, where `x` is a *global* section
because `U ⟶ U` is terminal there — is membership of `x` in the vanishing locus of `L|_U`.

Membership of `x` is not an `𝒪`-combination statement: by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.mem_generatedIdealSheaf_iff` the section `x` is only *locally* an
`𝒪`-linear combination of the generators, on a covering sieve `S` of `U`. So the argument has
three steps, one for each of the properties [Stacks, Tag 0998] asserts of the locus.

1. **Restriction stability**, `memVanishingIdeal_over_of_memVanishingIdeal`, applied twice:
   from `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_{f_i}, L) = 0` on the site to the same statement for `f_i|_W` and `L|_W`
   over the slice of the slice, `(𝒞/U)/(W ⟶ U)`, for `W ⟶ U` in `S`. The iterated slice is used
   as it stands, with no identification with `𝒞/W`: every statement consumed here holds at an
   arbitrary ringed site, and a slice of a ringed site is one.
2. **Multiplicativity and additivity**, `memVanishingIdeal_mulGlobalSection_of_memVanishingIdeal`
   and `memVanishingIdeal_addGlobalSection`, to pass from the generators to the combination
   `∑ c_i f_i|_W` that `x|_W` equals. The coefficients `c_i` are sections over `W` and are read
   as global sections of the iterated slice by
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfTerminalSection`.
3. **The sheaf condition**, `memVanishingIdeal_over_of_locally` of `VanishingIdealLocal.lean`,
   to pass from the members of `S` back to `U`. This is the step the source of
   [Stacks, Tag 0998] leaves to the reader.

## Implementation notes

The scalar at which [Stacks, Tag 0999] tests `L|_U` is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.terminalSectionToEnd ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).over U)`,
whereas the equivalence (1) ⇔ (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0997] is stated at
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.awaySmul` of the localized ringed site, whose sheaf of rings is
spelled `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.over U).O`. The two spellings denote one sheaf
of rings but instance search does not pass between them, so
`awaySmul_globalSectionOfTerminalSection` below is stated entirely in the second spelling — the
two sides of that equation are multiplication by one compatible family of local sections, read
in two ways — and the passage to the first happens only where the predicate is being discharged.

The four existential data of the predicate — additivity, exactness in both directions of
restriction to a slice, and the countable products of the derived category of the slice — are
supplied as in `NilpotentIdeal.lean`, from
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalCokernel.overFunctor_preservesFiniteLimits`, its colimit counterpart
and `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.hasProductsOfShape_nat_derivedCategory_over`. None of them is
a hypothesis on the site.

Nothing here carries a `stacks` attribute. The statement is the conjunction of the three clauses
of [Stacks, Tag 0998] — each registered where it is proved — with the local description of `ℐ`
from [Stacks, Tag 099B]; it is a hypothesis of that tag's reduction and not a clause of either
tag.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0999](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0999)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0998](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0998)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0997](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0997)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099B)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open scoped IsMulCommutative

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

section Sums

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})

/-- **The zero global section of the structure sheaf.** As with
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.addGlobalSection`, the type of global sections carries no additive
structure of its own, so the empty sum is formed here by hand.

It is `private`, and so are the statements below about it, because the public name
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.zeroGlobalSection` belongs to the more general declaration of
`CechDescentDatumObstruction.lean`, at a ringed site with three independent universe
parameters. That module is not in this one's import closure and reaching it would add some
hundred and seventy modules — the crystalline site and the divided-power development among them
— so the specialization is kept here and kept out of the public interface, where it would
collide. Nothing outside this module refers to it. -/
private def zeroGlobalSection : Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}) :=
  (Presheaf.globalSectionsEquivSections _).symm
    ⟨fun _ ↦ 0, fun {U _V} k ↦ by
      change (X.O.obj.map k).hom (0 : X.O.obj.obj U) = 0
      rw [map_zero]⟩

/-- The value of the zero global section over any object is zero. -/
private theorem globalSectionVal_zeroGlobalSection (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    globalSectionVal (zeroGlobalSection X) U = 0 := by
  simp [zeroGlobalSection, globalSectionVal]

/-- **A finite sum of global sections of the structure sheaf**, as a global section: its value
over an object is the sum of the values there. -/
def sumGlobalSection {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι)
    (a : ι → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u})) :
    Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}) :=
  (Presheaf.globalSectionsEquivSections _).symm
    ⟨fun U ↦ ∑ i ∈ s, globalSectionVal (a i) U, fun {U _V} k ↦ by
      change (X.O.obj.map k).hom (∑ i ∈ s, globalSectionVal (a i) U) = _
      rw [map_sum]
      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ globalSectionVal_map (a i) k⟩

/-- The value of `sumGlobalSection X s a` over an object is the sum over `s` of the values of the
`a i` there. -/
@[simp]
theorem globalSectionVal_sumGlobalSection {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι)
    (a : ι → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u})) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    globalSectionVal (sumGlobalSection X s a) U = ∑ i ∈ s, globalSectionVal (a i) U := by
  simp [sumGlobalSection, globalSectionVal]

/-- The value, over a terminal object, of the global section determined by a section there is
that section: the restriction is along the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfTerminalSection_self {T : X.C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (y : X.O.obj.obj (op T)) :
    globalSectionVal (globalSectionOfTerminalSection hT y) (op T) = y := by
  rw [globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfTerminalSection, hT.hom_ext (hT.from T) (𝟙 T)]
  simp

/-- **The value, over an object of the slice site, of a section over `U` read as a global
section there.** It is the restriction of the section along the structure map of that object. -/
theorem globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfTerminalSection_over (U : X.C) (x : X.O.obj.obj (op U))
    (V : (Over U)ᵒᵖ) :
    globalSectionVal (globalSectionOfTerminalSection (X := X.over U) Over.mkIdTerminal x) V =
      (X.O.obj.map V.unop.hom.op).hom x :=
  (globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfTerminalSection (X := X.over U) Over.mkIdTerminal x V).trans
    (congrArg (fun φ : V.unop ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 U) ↦ ((X.over U).O.obj.map φ.op).hom x)
      (Over.mkIdTerminal.hom_ext (Over.mkIdTerminal.from V.unop)
        (Over.homMk V.unop.hom : V.unop ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 U))))

/-- **An `𝒪`-linear identity between global sections holds everywhere as soon as it holds over a
terminal object of the site.** The restriction maps are ring homomorphisms and the values of a
global section over the objects of the site are a compatible family, so the identity propagates
from the terminal object along the unique arrows to it.

This is what lets the local-generation argument of [Stacks, Tag 099F] check its combination
identity at one object: over a slice site a section over `U` *is* a global section, and the
identity it satisfies there is the one the source writes down. -/
theorem globalSectionVal_eq_sum_mul_of_terminal {T : X.C} (hT : IsTerminal T) {r : ℕ}
    (b a : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
    (s : Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
    (hs : globalSectionVal s (op T) =
      ∑ i, globalSectionVal (b i) (op T) * globalSectionVal (a i) (op T))
    (V : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    globalSectionVal s V = ∑ i, globalSectionVal (b i) V * globalSectionVal (a i) V := by
  rw [← globalSectionVal_map s (hT.from V.unop).op, hs, map_sum]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ by
    rw [map_mul, globalSectionVal_map, globalSectionVal_map]

end Sums

section Locus

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u}) [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}]

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] linearCatCenterRingSheaf

/-- Multiplication by the zero global section is the zero endomorphism. -/
private theorem awaySmul_zeroGlobalSection : awaySmul X (zeroGlobalSection X) = 0 := by
  ext M V x
  rw [awaySmul_app_apply]
  simp [globalSectionVal_zeroGlobalSection, show ((0 : M ⟶ M)).val = 0 from rfl]

/-- **The zero global section lies in the vanishing locus of every object of `D(𝒪)`.** It is the
empty sum, so the closure of the locus under addition needs it; and it holds because `T(K, 0)` is
the invertibility of the identity. -/
private theorem memVanishingIdeal_zeroGlobalSection
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    MemVanishingIdeal X K (zeroGlobalSection X) :=
  (isZero_derivedSheafHom_derivedAwayModule_iff_isDerivedCompleteAt X _ K).2 <| by
    rw [awaySmul_zeroGlobalSection]
    exact isDerivedCompleteAt_of_isNilpotent (by rw [zero_smul]; exact IsNilpotent.zero)

/-- **The vanishing locus of [Stacks, Tag 0998] is closed under finite sums.** This is the
closure under addition, `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.memVanishingIdeal_addGlobalSection`,
iterated over a `Finset`, the empty sum being handled by `memVanishingIdeal_zeroGlobalSection`. -/
theorem memVanishingIdeal_sumGlobalSection
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    {ι : Type*}
    (a : ι → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u})) (s : Finset ι)
    (ha : ∀ i ∈ s, MemVanishingIdeal X K (a i)) :
    MemVanishingIdeal X K (sumGlobalSection X s a) := by
  classical
  induction s using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty =>
      rw [show sumGlobalSection X ∅ a = zeroGlobalSection X from
        globalSections_ext X fun V ↦ by simp [globalSectionVal_zeroGlobalSection]]
      exact memVanishingIdeal_zeroGlobalSection X K
  | insert j s hj ih =>
      rw [show sumGlobalSection X (insert j s) a =
          addGlobalSection X (a j) (sumGlobalSection X s a) from
        globalSections_ext X fun V ↦ by simp [Finset.sum_insert hj]]
      exact memVanishingIdeal_addGlobalSection X K _ _
        (ha j (Finset.mem_insert_self j s))
        (ih fun i hi ↦ ha i (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hi))

/-- **The vanishing locus of [Stacks, Tag 0998] contains every `𝒪`-linear combination of its
members.** If each `a_i` lies in the vanishing locus of `K` and the global section `s` has, over
every object, the value `∑ b_i a_i`, then `s` lies in the vanishing locus of `K`.

This is the closure under multiplication of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.memVanishingIdeal_mulGlobalSection_of_memVanishingIdeal` followed
by the closure under finite sums above; the coefficients `b_i` are arbitrary global sections and
nothing is assumed of them. -/
theorem memVanishingIdeal_of_eq_sum_mul
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) {r : ℕ}
    (b a : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
    (ha : ∀ i, MemVanishingIdeal X K (a i))
    (s : Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
    (hs : ∀ V : X.Cᵒᵖ, globalSectionVal s V =
      ∑ i, globalSectionVal (b i) V * globalSectionVal (a i) V) :
    MemVanishingIdeal X K s := by
  rw [show s = sumGlobalSection X Finset.univ (fun i ↦ mulGlobalSection X (b i) (a i)) from
    globalSections_ext X fun V ↦ by
      rw [hs V, globalSectionVal_sumGlobalSection]
      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦
        (globalSectionVal_mulGlobalSection X (b i) (a i) V).symm]
  exact memVanishingIdeal_sumGlobalSection X K _ _ fun i _ ↦
    memVanishingIdeal_mulGlobalSection_of_memVanishingIdeal X K _ _ (ha i)

/-- **Derived completeness along a sheaf of ideals is membership in the vanishing locus of the
restriction, at every local section of the ideal.** For an *arbitrary* sheaf of ideals
`ℐ ⊂ 𝒪`, an object `L` of `D(𝒪)` is derived complete along `ℐ` as soon as, for every object `U`
of the site and every section `x` of `ℐ` over `U`, the section `x` — read as a global section of
the structure sheaf of the localized ringed site `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.over X U`, where
`U ⟶ U` is terminal — lies in the vanishing locus of `L|_U`.

This is the implication (1) ⇒ (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0997], read at the localized ringed site and
propagated to the predicate of [Stacks, Tag 0999], together with the four existential data that
predicate carries: additivity of restriction to a slice, its exactness in both directions, and
the countable products of the derived category of the slice. None of those is a hypothesis on
the site.

It is the generic half of every argument that produces derived completeness along an ideal
sheaf: what is left to a caller is the vanishing-locus statement, which is where [Stacks, Tag
0998] does its work. `isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal` below
is this lemma with that work done for the ideal sheaf generated by finitely many global
sections, and the converse implication is
`memVanishingIdeal_over_of_isDerivedComplete`. -/
theorem isDerivedComplete_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal_over
    (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))
    (L : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    (hL : ∀ (U : X.C) (x : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj (op U)),
      x ∈ I.toSubmodule.obj (op U) →
        MemVanishingIdeal (X.over U)
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
            ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj L)
          (globalSectionOfTerminalSection (X := X.over U) Over.mkIdTerminal x)) :
    IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I L := by
  intro U x hx
  refine ⟨inferInstance,
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalCokernel.overFunctor_preservesFiniteLimits U,
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalCokernel.overFunctor_preservesFiniteColimits U,
    hasProductsOfShape_nat_derivedCategory_over.{u, u, u} X U, ?_⟩
  exact (isZero_derivedSheafHom_derivedAwayModule_iff_isDerivedCompleteAt (X.over U)
    (globalSectionOfTerminalSection (X := X.over U) Over.mkIdTerminal x) _).1 (hL U x hx)

/-- **A derived-complete object has every local section of the ideal sheaf in the vanishing
locus of its restriction.** This is the converse of
`isDerivedComplete_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal_over`: it is the implication (3) ⇒ (1) of
[Stacks, Tag 0997] applied to the condition the predicate of [Stacks, Tag 0999] asserts at the
object `U` and the section `x`.

It is the form in which a derived-completeness hypothesis is consumed by the three closure
properties of [Stacks, Tag 0998], all of which are stated for the vanishing locus. -/
theorem memVanishingIdeal_over_of_isDerivedComplete
    (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))
    {L : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))}
    (hL : IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I L) (U : X.C)
    {x : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj (op U)}
    (hx : x ∈ I.toSubmodule.obj (op U)) :
    MemVanishingIdeal (X.over U)
      ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
        ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj L)
      (globalSectionOfTerminalSection (X := X.over U) Over.mkIdTerminal x) := by
  obtain ⟨_, _, _, _, hc⟩ := hL U x hx
  exact (isZero_derivedSheafHom_derivedAwayModule_iff_isDerivedCompleteAt (X.over U)
    (globalSectionOfTerminalSection (X := X.over U) Over.mkIdTerminal x) _).2 hc

/-- **An object of `D(𝒪)` is derived complete along the ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r`
as soon as each generator lies in its vanishing locus.** That is: if
`R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_{f_i}, L) = 0` for every `i`, then `T(L|_U, x) = 0` for every object `U` of the
site and every section `x` of `ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r)` over `U`.

Nothing is assumed of `L`, of the sections or of the site. The three closure properties of
[Stacks, Tag 0998] and the local description of `ℐ` are what make the passage from the finitely
many generators to all local sections of `ℐ`; see the file's header for the shape of the
argument. -/
theorem isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal {r : ℕ}
    (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
    (L : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    (hL : ∀ i, MemVanishingIdeal X L (f i)) :
    IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X (generatedIdealSheaf f) L := by
  refine isDerivedComplete_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal_over X _ L fun U x hx ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hc⟩ := exists_sieve_of_mem_generatedIdealSheaf f hx
  exact memVanishingIdeal_over_of_locally X U
    ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) U).mapDerivedCategory.obj L)
    (globalSectionOfTerminalSection (X := X.over U) Over.mkIdTerminal x) hS
    fun W g hg ↦ by
      obtain ⟨c, hcW⟩ := hc g hg
      have hb : ∀ i, globalSectionVal (globalSectionOfTerminalSection
          (X := (X.over U).over (Over.mk g)) Over.mkIdTerminal (c i))
          (op (Over.mk (𝟙 (Over.mk g)))) = c i :=
        fun i ↦ globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfTerminalSection_self
          ((X.over U).over (Over.mk g)) Over.mkIdTerminal (c i)
      have ha : ∀ i, globalSectionVal (globalSectionOver (X.over U) (Over.mk g)
          (globalSectionOver X U (f i))) (op (Over.mk (𝟙 (Over.mk g)))) =
          globalSectionVal (f i) (op W) :=
        fun i ↦ (globalSectionVal_globalSectionOver (X.over U) (Over.mk g) _ _).trans
          (globalSectionVal_globalSectionOver X U (f i) _)
      have hx0 : globalSectionVal (globalSectionOver (X.over U) (Over.mk g)
          (globalSectionOfTerminalSection (X := X.over U) Over.mkIdTerminal x))
          (op (Over.mk (𝟙 (Over.mk g)))) = (X.O.obj.map g.op).hom x :=
        (globalSectionVal_globalSectionOver (X.over U) (Over.mk g) _ _).trans
          (globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfTerminalSection_over X U x (op (Over.mk g)))
      exact memVanishingIdeal_of_eq_sum_mul ((X.over U).over (Over.mk g)) _ _ _
        (fun i ↦ memVanishingIdeal_over_of_memVanishingIdeal (X.over U) (Over.mk g) _ _
          (memVanishingIdeal_over_of_memVanishingIdeal X U (f i) L (hL i))) _
        (globalSectionVal_eq_sum_mul_of_terminal ((X.over U).over (Over.mk g))
          Over.mkIdTerminal
          (fun i ↦ globalSectionOfTerminalSection
            (X := (X.over U).over (Over.mk g)) Over.mkIdTerminal (c i))
          (fun i ↦ globalSectionOver (X.over U) (Over.mk g) (globalSectionOver X U (f i))) _
          (hx0.trans (hcW.symm.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦
            (congrArg₂ (· * ·) (hb i) (ha i)).symm))))

end Locus

section Phi

attribute [local instance] hasMapBifunctor

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u}) [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}] {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] linearCatCenterRingSheaf

/-- **Each generator lies in the vanishing locus of the Čech completion.** For every `K` in
`D(𝒪)` and every `i`, `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_{f_i}, K^∧) = 0`, where
`K^∧ = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f), K)` is the candidate completion functor of [Stacks, Tag 099B].

This is the first half of the `hΦ` hypothesis of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion`. It is the
tensor–internal-Hom adjunction of [Stacks, Tag 08J9],
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_completionFunctor_of_isZero_derivedTensor`,
applied to the base-change vanishing `𝒪_{f_i} ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 Č(f) = 0` of
`isZero_derivedTensor_awayComplex_extendedAlternatingCech_prodGlobalSection`,
read at the singleton `{i}`. Nothing is assumed of `K` or of the sections. -/
theorem memVanishingIdeal_completionFunctor_obj
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    (i : Fin r) :
    MemVanishingIdeal X ((completionFunctor X f).obj K) (f i) := by
  refine isZero_derivedSheafHom_completionFunctor_of_isZero_derivedTensor X f _ K ?_
  have h := isZero_derivedTensor_awayComplex_extendedAlternatingCech_prodGlobalSection X f
    {i} i (Finset.mem_singleton_self i)
  rw [prodGlobalSection_singleton] at h
  exact h

/-- **The `hΦ` hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 099F], discharged**: every Čech completion
`K^∧ = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f), K)` is derived complete along the ideal sheaf
`ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r)` generated by the sections the Čech complex is built from.

It is `memVanishingIdeal_completionFunctor_obj` — the vanishing at the generators — followed by
`isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal`, which raises the vanishing
at the finitely many generators to the condition of [Stacks, Tag 0999] at every local section of
`ℐ`. Nothing is assumed of `K`, of the sections or of the site.

It is also the clause of [Stacks, Tag 099B] which asserts that the object `K^∧` the tag
constructs lies in `D_comp(𝒪)`; the universal property that makes it the left adjoint is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.bijective_precomp_completionUnit_generatedIdealSheaf` of
`GeneratedIdealAdjoint.lean`. -/
@[stacks 099B "that the Čech completion `K^∧ = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f), K)` lies in `D_comp(𝒪)`, at \
the ideal sheaf generated by the sections"]
theorem isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_completionFunctor_obj
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X (generatedIdealSheaf f) ((completionFunctor X f).obj K) :=
  isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal X f _
    (memVanishingIdeal_completionFunctor_obj X f K)

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 099F] for the ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r`, with `hΦ` and `hη` both
discharged.** The inclusion of the derived-complete objects into `D(𝒪)` has a left adjoint as
soon as the completion functor carries `K ⟶ K^∧` to `K^∧ ⟶ (K^∧)^∧`.

This is
`isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isDerivedComplete_completion`
with its first hypothesis proved rather than assumed, so that `hcomm` is the only remaining
input. That one is not a consequence of the other two: the two-object counterexample
`Stacks.Algebraization.CompletionUnitSharpness.exists_completionFunctor_and_not_isRightAdjoint_ι`
satisfies `hΦ` and `hη` and its inclusion has no left adjoint. It is, however, a consequence of
the other two together with the invertibility of `Φ η_K`, and both of those are proved in
`GeneratedIdealAdjoint.lean`: `hcomm` for this `(Φ, η)` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor_map_completionUnit_app` and the unconditional
statement of the tag is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf`, which
carries the `stacks` attribute. None is carried on this declaration, which still takes `hcomm`
as an input. -/
theorem isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_of_comm
    (hcomm : ∀ K, (completionFunctor X f).map ((completionUnit X f).app K) =
      (completionUnit X f).app ((completionFunctor X f).obj K)) :
    (ObjectProperty.ι
      (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X (generatedIdealSheaf f))).IsRightAdjoint :=
  isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isDerivedComplete_completion X f
    (isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_completionFunctor_obj X f) hcomm

end Phi

